    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Charnia masoni specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Charnia masoni" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Pass 1 does not claim the landscape disk resembles the cast.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters (0.14, 0.93, 0.062, 1.35) with the determinant-critical wavelength scaled to 0.0001404 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Charnia is a glide-reflected rangeomorph with apical growth (Brasier, Antcliffe and Liu 2012; Dunn et al. 2021); Ford 1958 named it from Charnwood Forest.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: 140 µm is the assigned detail tier, not a length measured on the fossil." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Charnia masoni (Late Ediacaran (565 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Charnia" ;
